          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "PSA.51"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ps 51",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "(Title)",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " sent the prophet Nathan to David. Nathan went to him and said, “There were two men who lived in the same town; one was rich and the other poor. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The rich man had many cattle and sheep, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "while the poor man had only one lamb, which he had bought. He took care of it, and it grew up in his home with his children. He would feed it with some of his own food, let it drink from his cup, and hold it in his lap. The lamb was like a daughter to him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "One day a visitor arrived at the rich man's home. The rich man didn't want to kill one of his own animals to prepare a meal for him; instead, he took the poor man's lamb and cooked a meal for his guest.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.4"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "David was very angry with the rich man and said, “I swear by the living ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " that the man who did this ought to die! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For having done such a cruel thing, he must pay back four times as much as he took.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“You are that man,” Nathan said to David. “And this is what the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " God of Israel says: ‘I made you king of Israel and rescued you from Saul. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I gave you his kingdom and his wives; I made you king over Israel and Judah. If this had not been enough, I would have given you twice as much. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Why, then, have you disobeyed my commands? Why did you do this evil thing? You had Uriah killed in battle; you let the Ammonites kill him, and then you took his wife! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now, in every generation some of your descendants will die a violent death because you have disobeyed me and have taken Uriah's wife. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2SA.16.22"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Sam 16.22",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I swear to you that I will cause someone from your own family to bring trouble on you. You will see it when I take your wives from you and give them to another man; and he will have intercourse with them in broad daylight. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You sinned in secret, but I will make this happen in broad daylight for all Israel to see.’ ”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“I have sinned against the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ",” David said.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.13"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Nathan replied, “The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " forgives you; you will not die. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But because you have shown such contempt for the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " in doing this, your child will die.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Nathan went home.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.15"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " caused the child that Uriah's wife had borne to David to become very ill. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "David prayed to God that the child would get well. He refused to eat anything, and every night he went into his room and spent the night lying on the floor. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "His court officials went to him and tried to make him get up, but he refused and would not eat anything with them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A week later the child died, and David's officials were afraid to tell him the news. They said, “While the child was living, David wouldn't answer us when we spoke to him. How can we tell him that his child is dead? He might do himself some harm!”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.18"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When David noticed them whispering to each other, he realized that the child had died. So he asked them, “Is the child dead?”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Yes, he is,” they answered.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "David got up from the floor, had a bath, combed his hair, and changed his clothes. Then he went and worshipped in the house of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". When he returned to the palace, he asked for food and ate it as soon as it was served. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“We don't understand this,” his officials said to him. “While the child was alive, you wept for him and would not eat; but as soon as he died, you got up and ate!”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.21"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Yes,” David answered, “I did fast and weep while he was still alive. I thought that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " might be merciful to me and not let the child die. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But now that he is dead, why should I fast? Could I bring the child back to life? I will some day go to where he is, but he can never come back to me.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.23"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then David comforted his wife Bathsheba. He had intercourse with her, and she bore a son, whom David named Solomon. The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " loved the boy ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and commanded the prophet Nathan to name the boy Jedidiah,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12.25",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Jedidiah",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": ": This name in Hebrew means “Beloved of the LORD”.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " because the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " loved him.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.25"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Meanwhile Joab continued his campaign against Rabbah, the capital city of Ammon, and was about to capture it. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He sent messengers to David to report: “I have attacked Rabbah and have captured its water supply. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now gather the rest of your forces, attack the city and take it yourself. I don't want to get the credit for capturing it.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So David gathered his forces, went to Rabbah, attacked it, and conquered it. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "From the head of the idol of the Ammonite god Molech",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12.30",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "idol of the Ammonite god Molech",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; or",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Ammonite king.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " David took a gold crown which weighed about 35 kilogrammes and had a jewel in it. David took the jewel and put it in his own crown.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12.30",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "jewel",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "…",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "crown",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; or",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "crown and put it on his own head.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " He also took a large amount of loot from the city ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 12:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and put its people to work with saws, iron hoes, and iron axes, and forced them to work at",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12.31",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Probable text (see 1 Chr 20.3)",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "work at",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; Hebrew",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "pass through.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " making bricks. He did the same to the people of all the other towns of Ammon. Then he and his men returned to Jerusalem.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.12.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.12.31"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
